(7257459, 1127631, 100393, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> I can''t figure out what I''m looking at!!! Reminds me of Nixter''s masterpiece<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=997554" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1517/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_997554.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1517/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_997554.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1517/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_997554.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Praise indeed! I can see the similarity, although my gut doesn''t flip when I look at mine! His is casual and visceral at the same time. It seems to hit multiple sweet spots in my brain.</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: I can''t figure out what I''m looking at!!! Reminds me of Nixter''s masterpiece    Praise indeed! I can see the similarity, although my gut doesn''t flip when I look at mine! His is casual and visceral at the same time. It seems to hit multiple sweet spots in my brain.', '2014-09-01 14:46:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7257532, 1127753, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I can see why you would enjoy this spot in Yellowstone.  Not only did you see the majestic fall of water, you got to hear the roar of sound and perhaps even gather in a bit of the mist.<br/> <br/>Now, you had some trouble managing your darks and lights, which is why it''s a good idea to bracket your shots, if your camera will do it.<br/> <br/>As it is, your waterfall loses detail and could be described in part as "hot" while the trees, especially those to the right are so dark as to be lost among the rocks.  In addition, that lovely waterfall is smack in the middle of your composition.  while sometimes this works, it would have been fun to see an image where the waterfall was over to the right cascading into the frame.  <br/> <br/>So, I''d consider this more of a ''record'' shot.  Once you have that one, experiment a lot and get different angles and exposures.  You will be pleasantly surprised.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  I can see why you would enjoy this spot in Yellowstone.  Not only did you see the majestic fall of water, you got to hear the roar of sound and perhaps even gather in a bit of the mist. Now, you had some trouble managing your darks and lights, which is why it''s a good idea to bracket your shots, if your camera will do it. As it is, your waterfall loses detail and could be described in part as "hot" while the trees, especially those to the right are so dark as to be lost among the rocks.  In addition, that lovely waterfall is smack in the middle of your composition.  while sometimes this works, it would have been fun to see an image where the waterfall was over to the right cascading into the frame.   So, I''d consider this more of a ''record'' shot.  Once you have that one, experiment a lot and get different angles and exposures.  You will be pleasantly surprised.', '2014-09-01 20:48:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7257533, 1127866, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=175381" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">clickodak</a>!  I get to look at one of your images in depth again!  Delightful!<br/> <br/>Your powers of observation are magical.  To see something like this is a gift.  Hang on to  that gift.<br/> <br/>Now, personally I liked the image alot.  For the Challenge, I was bothered a bit by the white outline.  <br/>Frankly, I think that black border (eliminating the white) would have met the Challenge equally as well, and perhaps would have  scored better. <br/> <br/>Technically, nothing wrong with this image - or at least that I can tell.<br/> <br/>I do like your sense of originality, in all your Challenge submissions. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club   clickodak!  I get to look at one of your images in depth again!  Delightful! Your powers of observation are magical.  To see something like this is a gift.  Hang on to  that gift. Now, personally I liked the image alot.  For the Challenge, I was bothered a bit by the white outline.  Frankly, I think that black border (eliminating the white) would have met the Challenge equally as well, and perhaps would have  scored better.  Technically, nothing wrong with this image - or at least that I can tell. I do like your sense of originality, in all your Challenge submissions.  ', '2014-09-01 20:54:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7257535, 1128135, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Oh, Janine,  so much going on in this image.  <br/> <br/>As an advertisement for a, what, movie?  tv show? it probably works, but for DPC?  Not much original content.<br/> <br/>I look at the framing and wonder if it is the edge of a tv screen or the edge of a billboard.  In either case,<br/>well, not much there in the framing department.  Is the guardrail your find?  If so, that knits the composition<br/>together somewhat.  <br/> <br/>Still it pleased enough of our voters to keep you above a 5.0 and that''s something.  <br/> <br/>Hope all is well with you, these days.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Oh, Janine,  so much going on in this image.   As an advertisement for a, what, movie?  tv show? it probably works, but for DPC?  Not much original content. I look at the framing and wonder if it is the edge of a tv screen or the edge of a billboard.  In either case,well, not much there in the framing department.  Is the guardrail your find?  If so, that knits the compositiontogether somewhat.   Still it pleased enough of our voters to keep you above a 5.0 and that''s something.   Hope all is well with you, these days.', '2014-09-01 21:04:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7257538, 1128133, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=7810" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Coley</a>!  good to see your work back in the Challenges.<br/> <br/>As usual, a masterful take on the Challenge, with that light path framed so well, in letterbox fashion with darks.<br/> <br/>While this had a respectable score, it might have done even better had you blocked out the sky and just left the lake and trees and hills to frame your paddler.  <br/> <br/>Other than that, it''s serene and lovely.  what''s not to like.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club   Coley!  good to see your work back in the Challenges. As usual, a masterful take on the Challenge, with that light path framed so well, in letterbox fashion with darks. While this had a respectable score, it might have done even better had you blocked out the sky and just left the lake and trees and hills to frame your paddler.   Other than that, it''s serene and lovely.  what''s not to like.', '2014-09-01 21:58:03.000000', NULL, 0),
